,"prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A condition that applicants must meet is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v73cf1ea9b9f1","label":"suggestion that can always be ignored"},{"id":"vfeb76f0447b5","label":"receipt"},{"id":"v3015c6bcbd49","label":"requirement"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3015c6bcbd49"},"reference_answer":"v3015c6bcbd49","incorrect_answer":"v73cf1ea9b9f1","explanation":"Requirement — обязательное условие для заявки."},{"id":"327c6f89-97db-52e4-8ec0-36d844ff244e","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: At this time tomorrow, we ___ the equipment, so we will not be available.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"ve6733dc7cd22","label":"will be testing"},{"id":"v49d334cee871","label":"will testing"},{"id":"vd975365b1998","label":"will be test"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve6733dc7cd22"},"reference_answer":"ve6733dc7cd22","incorrect_answer":"v49d334cee871","explanation":"Will be testing показывает процесс в указанный будущий момент."},{"id":"c066331d-f225-589f-9cc2-7958b1127f2c","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: checked / checking.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"At noon, the technicians will be ___ the new system."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["checking"]},"reference_answer":"checking","incorrect_answer":"checked","explanation":"После will be в Future Continuous требуется checking."},{"id":"536fbd4e-0138-5c3f-ae69-e7ba982fd315","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «В десять мы будем проверять оборудование.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"be"},{"id":"t4","label":"testing"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"equipment"},{"id":"t7","label":"at"},{"id":"t8","label":"ten."},{"id":"t1","label":"We"},{"id":"t2","label":"will"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Будущий процесс не равен обещанию закончить проверку к десяти."},{"id":"d25e8486-0e93-56d9-9a58-dc09c6d2146f","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь указанную конструкцию, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"At three tomorrow, she will working with the volunteers."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["At three tomorrow, she will be working with the volunteers."]},"reference_answer":"At three tomorrow, she will be working with the volunteers.","incorrect_answer":"At three tomorrow, she will working with the volunteers.","explanation":"Для будущего продолженного времени между will и working требуется be."},{"id":"9877ed63-1642-517e-a782-77ba50b44e68","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему команда не могла созвониться в два?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A research team scheduled a live demonstration for Thursday afternoon. When a visitor requested a call at two, the coordinator explained that they would be testing the equipment at that time. The visitor suggested three instead. The coordinator accepted provisionally, noting that testing might run longer if faults appeared. The schedule described what would be in progress at two; it did not guarantee that all tests would have been completed by three. The team promised to confirm availability once the morning checks were finished.","options":[{"id":"ve89691977eaa","label":"Every test was guaranteed to be finished before noon."},{"id":"v132bddae6d20","label":"The visitor had cancelled the demonstration."},{"id":"v48b38b15416a","label":"Equipment testing would be in progress."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v48b38b15416a"},"reference_answer":"v48b38b15416a","incorrect_answer":"ve89691977eaa","explanation":"Будущий процесс в два часа препятствовал звонку."},{"id":"9b736d2e-8d63-5302-a237-223f2b5e1b08","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова урока с переводом в указанном контексте.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l6def0a6852e0","label":"in progress"},{"id":"l7e25d7ad9bd1","label":"shift"},{"id":"l66cc18ef0a6b","label":"available"},{"id":"l3a7991ee4501","label":"reschedule"}],"right":[{"id":"r42f7636fcd22","label":"свободный по времени"},{"id":"rb197d852923e","label":"перенести"},{"id":"rb1cbb45b75d4","label":"в процессе"},{"id":"r0d43cf8fdc74","label":"рабочая смена"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l6def0a6852e0":"rb1cbb45b75d4","l7e25d7ad9bd1":"r0d43cf8fdc74","l66cc18ef0a6b":"r42f7636fcd22","l3a7991ee4501":"rb197d852923e"}},"reference_answer":{"l6def0a6852e0":"rb1cbb45b75d4","l7e25d7ad9bd1":"r0d43cf8fdc74","l66cc18ef0a6b":"r42f7636fcd22","l3a7991ee4501":"rb197d852923e"},"incorrect_answer":{"l6def0a6852e0":"r0d43cf8fdc74","l7e25d7ad9bd1":"rb1cbb45b75d4","l66cc18ef0a6b":"r42f7636fcd22","l3a7991ee4501":"rb197d852923e"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: in progress — в процессе; shift — рабочая смена; available — свободный по времени; reschedule — перенести."},{"id":"6a5ae917-af45-5f86-acee-75fda512e1be","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой статус у договорённости на три?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A research team scheduled a live demonstration for Thursday afternoon. When a visitor requested a call at two, the coordinator explained that they would be testing the equipment at that time. The visitor suggested three instead. The coordinator accepted provisionally, noting that testing might run longer if faults appeared. The schedule described what would be in progress at two; it did not guarantee that all tests would have been completed by three. The team promised to confirm availability once the morning checks were finished.","options":[{"id":"v053ecbfe43eb","label":"Rejected without any alternative."},{"id":"v22e5e10b1613","label":"Provisional, because testing could overrun."},{"id":"v83ac8294cb78","label":"Guaranteed regardless of faults."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v22e5e10b1613"},"reference_answer":"v22e5e10b1613","incorrect_answer":"v83ac8294cb78","explanation":"Предварительное согласие связано с возможностью затянувшейся проверки."},{"id":"c7781674-78bf-55cb-b1c4-e1c4d1e0ca6b","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Укажи будущий процесс и предложи другое время.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we call you at ten tomorrow?"}],"options":[{"id":"v0b3848d54d9c","label":"I will travelling then; could we speak at noon?"},{"id":"v46123799f6eb","label":"I will be travel then; could we speak at noon?"},{"id":"v7d0aa3553a73","label":"I will be travelling then; could we speak at noon?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7d0aa3553a73"},"reference_answer":"v7d0aa3553a73","incorrect_answer":"v0b3848d54d9c","explanation":"Will be travelling — правильная форма Future Continuous."},{"id":"f04fb299-2e0d-51c4-b501-137e737c3d20","lesson_id":"f2351746-caa6-589b-a69f-ef7cfc83650d","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If a task is still happening, it is ___.","options":[{"id":"v051a93945e90","label":"cancelled by definition"},{"id":"vc9e060f62857","label":"in progress"},{"id":"vb4ebed148711","label":"completed beyond doubt"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc9e060f62857"},"reference_answer":"vc9e060f62857","incorrect_answer":"vb4ebed148711","explanation":"In progress означает продолжающееся выполнение."},{"id":"019d63b8-8c36-59fe-85fa-ce5def3873c2","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: They ___ for an hour when the doors finally opened.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vb859c7311d88","label":"had waiting"},{"id":"v8fe8fa3c8516","label":"have been waited"},{"id":"v018fc9877677","label":"had been waiting"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v018fc9877677"},"reference_answer":"v018fc9877677","incorrect_answer":"vb859c7311d88","explanation":"Длительный процесс до момента в прошлом выражается had been waiting."},{"id":"0eca354d-a950-5433-983f-971f930b60d8","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: investigating / investigated.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The team had been ___ the fault all morning before the cause was found."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["investigating"]},"reference_answer":"investigating","incorrect_answer":"investigated","explanation":"После had been для активного процесса нужна investigating."},{"id":"b755b12e-eb44-50dd-b866-e366b20e5f0b","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «К моменту прибытия она ехала всю ночь.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"been"},{"id":"t4","label":"travelling"},{"id":"t5","label":"all"},{"id":"t6","label":"night"},{"id":"t7","label":"when"},{"id":"t8","label":"she"},{"id":"t9","label":"arrived."},{"id":"t1","label":"She"},{"id":"t2","label":"had"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Had been travelling связывает длительный процесс с последующим прошлым событием."},{"id":"e95c8970-2a2c-5b21-b937-67bdfc3e8255","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь указанную конструкцию, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We had been waited for two hours when help arrived."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We had been waiting for two hours when help arrived."]},"reference_answer":"We had been waiting for two hours when help arrived.","incorrect_answer":"We had been waited for two hours when help arrived.","explanation":"В активном Past Perfect Continuous требуется waiting."},{"id":"8d558047-9a26-5c67-915c-6f174d6af1f5","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как долго волонтёры работали к полудню?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The volunteers looked exhausted when the event manager arrived at noon. They had been arranging the outdoor stalls since seven, and a delivery delay had forced them to move several tables twice. The manager first assumed that the work had been poorly planned. After hearing the sequence of events, she realised that an unexpected missing delivery had added to the workload. She brought in two extra helpers rather than criticising the volunteers on the basis of their tired appearance alone.","options":[{"id":"v0a676c42e73b","label":"For exactly two days."},{"id":"v92002ee5cd00","label":"Since seven that morning, about five hours."},{"id":"vc3a14357c5dd","label":"Only since the manager arrived."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v92002ee5cd00"},"reference_answer":"v92002ee5cd00","incorrect_answer":"vc3a14357c5dd","explanation":"Начало в семь и прибытие в полдень задают около пяти часов."},{"id":"38b7cc8e-86c6-50d4-997d-eeacb6b4daf6","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова урока с переводом в указанном контексте.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1532e1af10db","label":"queue"},{"id":"lced107a4aef7","label":"delay"},{"id":"l69219999b413","label":"exhausted"},{"id":"ld2fa112abdc3","label":"eventually"}],"right":[{"id":"r5ab512276c06","label":"измотанный"},{"id":"r2b9c69c31017","label":"в конце концов"},{"id":"rb822f6ea7929","label":"очередь"},{"id":"r0b2f136beeed","label":"задержка"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1532e1af10db":"rb822f6ea7929","lced107a4aef7":"r0b2f136beeed","l69219999b413":"r5ab512276c06","ld2fa112abdc3":"r2b9c69c31017"}},"reference_answer":{"l1532e1af10db":"rb822f6ea7929","lced107a4aef7":"r0b2f136beeed","l69219999b413":"r5ab512276c06","ld2fa112abdc3":"r2b9c69c31017"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1532e1af10db":"r0b2f136beeed","lced107a4aef7":"rb822f6ea7929","l69219999b413":"r5ab512276c06","ld2fa112abdc3":"r2b9c69c31017"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: queue — очередь; delay — задержка; exhausted — измотанный; eventually — в конце концов."},{"id":"a7c12b81-7146-5b8e-a990-45b528048705","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как изменилась оценка менеджера?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The volunteers looked exhausted when the event manager arrived at noon. They had been arranging the outdoor stalls since seven, and a delivery delay had forced them to move several tables twice. The manager first assumed that the work had been poorly planned. After hearing the sequence of events, she realised that an unexpected missing delivery had added to the workload. She brought in two extra helpers rather than criticising the volunteers on the basis of their tired appearance alone.","options":[{"id":"v8aa723cbe568","label":"She recognised an additional workload caused by an unexpected delay."},{"id":"ve6bc09b0a397","label":"She proved that tiredness always means poor planning."},{"id":"v0ff8d9e119f9","label":"She cancelled the work without hearing any explanation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8aa723cbe568"},"reference_answer":"v8aa723cbe568","incorrect_answer":"ve6bc09b0a397","explanation":"Выяснение последовательности событий изменило исходное предположение."},{"id":"b29842d0-7d74-56cb-97df-84711d6b5c7a","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Объясни усталость процессом, предшествующим прибытию.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Why was the team so tired when you arrived?"}],"options":[{"id":"v50ace0126229","label":"They have been moved equipment tomorrow."},{"id":"vbe56c01510a9","label":"They had been moving equipment since dawn."},{"id":"v101b4e5b5729","label":"They had moving equipment since dawn."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbe56c01510a9"},"reference_answer":"vbe56c01510a9","incorrect_answer":"v101b4e5b5729","explanation":"Had been moving выражает длительную активную работу до прошлого момента."},{"id":"c2320197-45c8-508b-97ca-119c5dd98ead","lesson_id":"b78e8e4b-3dbd-59a8-bb66-b8a8ef3b6526","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Extremely tired after sustained effort means ___.","options":[{"id":"v6313744e9fc1","label":"exhausted"},{"id":"vf8a8e630ebe2","label":"available"},{"id":"v616dba6cf796","label":"unaffected"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v6313744e9fc1"},"reference_answer":"v6313744e9fc1","incorrect_answer":"vf8a8e630ebe2","explanation":"Exhausted — сильная усталость, а не просто занятость или доступность."},{"id":"0150900f-6b7a-54c3-86b0-67d95641f470","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: They objected to ___ from the discussion.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v7e321d2f44af","label":"be excluded"},{"id":"vf7755dca53de","label":"being excluded"},{"id":"v9634136c05a9","label":"being exclude"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf7755dca53de"},"reference_answer":"vf7755dca53de","incorrect_answer":"v9634136c05a9","explanation":"После to как предлога в objected to нужен пассивный герундий being excluded."},{"id":"629e966f-6ddf-59b4-be2f-570df775517a","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: informing / informed.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The schedule changed without anyone being ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["informed"]},"reference_answer":"informed","incorrect_answer":"informing","explanation":"Людей уведомляют, поэтому пассивное being informed."},{"id":"ea1e2ad1-16d0-5114-a690-0d0b17838a7e","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Ей не нравилось, когда её прерывали во время объяснения.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"being"},{"id":"t4","label":"interrupted"},{"id":"t5","label":"during"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"explanation."},{"id":"t1","label":"She"},{"id":"t2","label":"disliked"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Being interrupted указывает, что прерывают её, а не она сама прерывает других."},{"id":"5ff0cabb-fae1-547b-b3fc-e3f9432b9939","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь указанную конструкцию, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"He complained about being ignore during the meeting."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["He complained about being ignored during the meeting."]},"reference_answer":"He complained about being ignored during the meeting.","incorrect_answer":"He complained about being ignore during the meeting.","explanation":"В пассивном герундии после being требуется причастие ignored."},{"id":"6b3afe27-5e7f-5ce6-b1b5-3f841a35c0b9","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему группа могла не узнать о встрече?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A neighbourhood group complained about being excluded from a planning discussion. The organiser replied that the meeting had been advertised online. However, several regular participants used a printed noticeboard rather than the website, and no notice had been placed there. The group did not demand that every decision be reversed immediately. It asked for a chance to comment before the final recommendation was submitted. The disagreement concerned meaningful participation, not merely whether a notice technically existed somewhere.","options":[{"id":"vb463de7babbc","label":"Some members relied on a noticeboard that had no announcement."},{"id":"v884be61744a9","label":"The organiser had never advertised it anywhere."},{"id":"vb868dcdb5d58","label":"Every member had already read the online notice."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb463de7babbc"},"reference_answer":"vb463de7babbc","incorrect_answer":"v884be61744a9","explanation":"Онлайн-объявление существовало, но привычный канал части участников не использовался."},{"id":"e5fa8a59-3d62-5787-97b4-a21cb2d9ad52","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова урока с переводом в указанном контексте.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"le71780cdc51f","label":"inform"},{"id":"lc8535167917c","label":"consult"},{"id":"lbca0718841fc","label":"exclude"},{"id":"lee1b86689839","label":"notice"}],"right":[{"id":"r6ac715a84754","label":"исключать"},{"id":"rb59f599fc1cf","label":"уведомление"},{"id":"raaeac21849ad","label":"уведомлять"},{"id":"rd0f571651bb4","label":"советоваться"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"le71780cdc51f":"raaeac21849ad","lc8535167917c":"rd0f571651bb4","lbca0718841fc":"r6ac715a84754","lee1b86689839":"rb59f599fc1cf"}},"reference_answer":{"le71780cdc51f":"raaeac21849ad","lc8535167917c":"rd0f571651bb4","lbca0718841fc":"r6ac715a84754","lee1b86689839":"rb59f599fc1cf"},"incorrect_answer":{"le71780cdc51f":"rd0f571651bb4","lc8535167917c":"raaeac21849ad","lbca0718841fc":"r6ac715a84754","lee1b86689839":"rb59f599fc1cf"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: inform — уведомлять; consult — советоваться; exclude — исключать; notice — уведомление."},{"id":"1e405ae4-0350-51b2-aa85-83aaa7e611ae","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"reading","prompt":"Чего группа просила?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A neighbourhood group complained about being excluded from a planning discussion. The organiser replied that the meeting had been advertised online. However, several regular participants used a printed noticeboard rather than the website, and no notice had been placed there. The group did not demand that every decision be reversed immediately. It asked for a chance to comment before the final recommendation was submitted. The disagreement concerned meaningful participation, not merely whether a notice technically existed somewhere.","options":[{"id":"v15673cdf1243","label":"Immediate reversal of every decision without discussion."},{"id":"ve4c593827e22","label":"A permanent end to all online announcements."},{"id":"v1108d924066b","label":"An opportunity to comment before the final recommendation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1108d924066b"},"reference_answer":"v1108d924066b","incorrect_answer":"v15673cdf1243","explanation":"Просьба касается участия до окончательной рекомендации, а не немедленной отмены всего."},{"id":"d57edf5a-43e1-51fa-b390-83401937c792","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Вырази, что тебя не уведомили.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Did they tell you about the changed venue?"}],"options":[{"id":"v4bd01380307b","label":"No. I arrived without being informed of the change."},{"id":"v8b4d7bafb7e0","label":"No. I arrived without being inform of the change."},{"id":"vb94706d23ba0","label":"No. I arrived without be informed of the change."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4bd01380307b"},"reference_answer":"v4bd01380307b","incorrect_answer":"v8b4d7bafb7e0","explanation":"Without being informed — пассивный герундий после without."},{"id":"da5895db-6589-57a8-95b1-f13fbb9b75f5","lesson_id":"3b2e3f6e-69bb-538a-8ee8-83102373a2cd","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To leave someone out of a discussion is to ___ them.","options":[{"id":"v927d4729eed6","label":"consult"},{"id":"v2c466e7b9544","label":"inform"},{"id":"v4d2bef3caf30","label":"exclude"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4d2bef3caf30"},"reference_answer":"v4d2bef3caf30","incorrect_answer":"v927d4729eed6","explanation":"Exclude — исключить из участия, в отличие от совета или уведомления."},{"id":"c293f47b-f19f-51d0-8473-58083bf9ec40","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: They repeatedly leave the door open. I wish they ___ it.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v05252163e5e1","label":"would close"},{"id":"vfc821e63a61b","label":"would closed"},{"id":"v0f0e7f36b8aa","label":"had closing"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v05252163e5e1"},"reference_answer":"v05252163e5e1","incorrect_answer":"vfc821e63a61b","explanation":"Would close выражает желаемое изменение повторяющегося поведения."},{"id":"493d9ddb-8c6a-53a5-93fa-a79dd5149a1d","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: lower / lowered.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I wish the neighbours would ___ the volume after midnight."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["lower"]},"reference_answer":"lower","incorrect_answer":"lowered","explanation":"После would нужна начальная форма lower."},{"id":"77ab1654-38fc-5d19-9c97-d50147004a5c","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Хотелось бы, чтобы они начали отвечать на наши сообщения.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"they"},{"id":"t4","label":"would"},{"id":"t5","label":"respond"},{"id":"t6","label":"to"},{"id":"t7","label":"our"},{"id":"t8","label":"messages."},{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"wish"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Would respond выражает желаемое изменение, а не утверждает, что ответы уже были."},{"id":"8ab0b77a-8aba-516a-8bd6-cee35b9e505d","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь указанную конструкцию, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I wish he would stops interrupting."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I wish he would stop interrupting."]},"reference_answer":"I wish he would stop interrupting.","incorrect_answer":"I wish he would stops interrupting.","explanation":"После would используется stop без -s."},{"id":"4abeeb7d-e7a1-5d0c-ac82-003c4d9da905","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое изменение поведения требуется?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A tenant had asked several times for the shared entrance to be kept clear. Bicycles were still being left across the doorway, making access difficult. In a message to the residents, she wrote, “I wish everyone would use the bicycle store.” She was asking for a change in current behaviour, not claiming that the store had always been available in the past. The building manager then checked whether all residents had keys to it before repeating the request.","options":[{"id":"v6f0fcb40f018","label":"Removing the doorway permanently."},{"id":"vf1fbdf55984f","label":"Stopping residents from entering their homes."},{"id":"v85b2ed96aa24","label":"Keeping bicycles in the store rather than across the doorway."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v85b2ed96aa24"},"reference_answer":"v85b2ed96aa24","incorrect_answer":"v6f0fcb40f018","explanation":"Желаемое изменение — использовать помещение для велосипедов."},{"id":"2ac1c432-354a-55fe-b2b4-ef99c50bd9e1","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова урока с переводом в указанном контексте.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l7a634c377660","label":"persistent"},{"id":"l25d55e39676c","label":"disturb"},{"id":"l532014ef79be","label":"considerate"},{"id":"l3f4b5479ccab","label":"respond"}],"right":[{"id":"rc5d35be04c56","label":"внимательный к другим"},{"id":"r7d8af774986f","label":"отвечать"},{"id":"r32abeeb2c2a3","label":"постоянно повторяющийся"},{"id":"r15dda26fb29a","label":"мешать"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l7a634c377660":"r32abeeb2c2a3","l25d55e39676c":"r15dda26fb29a","l532014ef79be":"rc5d35be04c56","l3f4b5479ccab":"r7d8af774986f"}},"reference_answer":{"l7a634c377660":"r32abeeb2c2a3","l25d55e39676c":"r15dda26fb29a","l532014ef79be":"rc5d35be04c56","l3f4b5479ccab":"r7d8af774986f"},"incorrect_answer":{"l7a634c377660":"r15dda26fb29a","l25d55e39676c":"r32abeeb2c2a3","l532014ef79be":"rc5d35be04c56","l3f4b5479ccab":"r7d8af774986f"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: persistent — постоянно повторяющийся; disturb — мешать; considerate — внимательный к другим; respond — отвечать."},{"id":"140c3b8d-67f7-50f5-bacf-3081131cce25","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"reading","prompt":"Зачем менеджер проверил наличие ключей?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A tenant had asked several times for the shared entrance to be kept clear. Bicycles were still being left across the doorway, making access difficult. In a message to the residents, she wrote, “I wish everyone would use the bicycle store.” She was asking for a change in current behaviour, not claiming that the store had always been available in the past. The building manager then checked whether all residents had keys to it before repeating the request.","options":[{"id":"v7d0afa3529be","label":"To establish that the past could be changed."},{"id":"v0e2342ff6cad","label":"To check whether residents could actually use the proposed alternative."},{"id":"vf9d6db9d3507","label":"To prove that everyone had deliberately ignored the tenant."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0e2342ff6cad"},"reference_answer":"v0e2342ff6cad","incorrect_answer":"vf9d6db9d3507","explanation":"Доступность альтернативы нельзя молча считать одинаковой для всех."},{"id":"e2ae38c9-1e80-5d2c-aa2c-b0bd1b2edb2c","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Вырази желание изменить нынешнюю практику ответов.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"The office never answers our calls promptly."}],"options":[{"id":"v8d5df36cafc7","label":"I wish they would responded more quickly."},{"id":"vb059ec181063","label":"I wish they will responding more quickly."},{"id":"v5fef0cc11670","label":"I wish they would respond more quickly."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5fef0cc11670"},"reference_answer":"v5fef0cc11670","incorrect_answer":"v8d5df36cafc7","explanation":"Wish they would respond соответствует просьбе об изменении поведения."},{"id":"70d8ccba-ad1f-53c6-a5af-a0f3a55ac597","lesson_id":"8dea2842-7a8c-5fbc-b76f-ac362f393b80","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Repeated noise that makes it hard to work can ___ people.","options":[{"id":"v4b2912af1b0b","label":"reimburse"},{"id":"v396b83353929","label":"disturb"},{"id":"vbe39eaa9bcc3","label":"certify"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v396b83353929"},"reference_answer":"v396b83353929","incorrect_answer":"vbe39eaa9bcc3","explanation":"Disturb — мешать или нарушать покой."},{"id":"1625391f-c9f6-5f59-b616-c95554d204a3","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The route is flooded. You had better ___ the road report before leaving.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vcd62cc95c32e","label":"to check"},{"id":"ve04d6c4f82fb","label":"checking"},{"id":"v20cdc1b719df","label":"check"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v20cdc1b719df"},"reference_answer":"v20cdc1b719df","incorrect_answer":"vcd62cc95c32e","explanation":"После had better нужен инфинитив без to; контекст даёт вескую причину совета."},{"id":"3b658f3a-f9fc-58ce-8e71-0946bcf1f131","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: waiting / wait.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I would rather ___ until we have more information."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["wait"]},"reference_answer":"wait","incorrect_answer":"waiting","explanation":"После would rather в этой конструкции используется wait."},{"id":"296044bb-fe08-5537-baba-243755b5b329","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Тебе лучше не игнорировать предупреждение.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"better"},{"id":"t4","label":"not"},{"id":"t5","label":"ignore"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"warning."},{"id":"t1","label":"You"},{"id":"t2","label":"had"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Отрицание ставится после had better и перед смысловым глаголом."},{"id":"04c30ea6-4d45-5f48-ba77-7f63064cbb83","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь указанную конструкцию, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I would rather to speak to the organiser first."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I would rather speak to the organiser first."]},"reference_answer":"I would rather speak to the organiser first.","incorrect_answer":"I would rather to speak to the organiser first.","explanation":"После would rather лишнее to убирается."},{"id":"0531c2b6-9012-53a7-801f-308255d74518","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какая реплика выражает предпочтение?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"Two colleagues were choosing how to reach a training centre after heavy rain. One said she would rather take the train than drive. The other preferred driving because of the equipment they needed to carry. Before deciding, their manager warned that the main road might be flooded and said they had better check the travel updates. The advice did not remove their choice of transport, but it made checking the conditions important before acting on either preference.","options":[{"id":"v41bc09cbaba8","label":"The main road might be flooded."},{"id":"v47436636bb02","label":"She would rather take the train."},{"id":"ve1096aa251bd","label":"They had better check the travel updates."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v47436636bb02"},"reference_answer":"v47436636bb02","incorrect_answer":"ve1096aa251bd","explanation":"Would rather обозначает предпочтение; had better — совет, might — возможность."},{"id":"b08137ca-4003-56be-b82c-d70fb8d7f962","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова урока с переводом в указанном контексте.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lb3abe1914412","label":"preference"},{"id":"lca6ea4585aac","label":"advice"},{"id":"l2dff74723f73","label":"consequence"},{"id":"l89b64e040b0d","label":"urgent"}],"right":[{"id":"ra252e9d166ba","label":"последствие"},{"id":"r4294538e93ac","label":"срочный"},{"id":"r37cfc07a1b15","label":"предпочтение"},{"id":"r98ddbb296f16","label":"совет"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lb3abe1914412":"r37cfc07a1b15","lca6ea4585aac":"r98ddbb296f16","l2dff74723f73":"ra252e9d166ba","l89b64e040b0d":"r4294538e93ac"}},"reference_answer":{"lb3abe1914412":"r37cfc07a1b15","lca6ea4585aac":"r98ddbb296f16","l2dff74723f73":"ra252e9d166ba","l89b64e040b0d":"r4294538e93ac"},"incorrect_answer":{"lb3abe1914412":"r98ddbb296f16","lca6ea4585aac":"r37cfc07a1b15","l2dff74723f73":"ra252e9d166ba","l89b64e040b0d":"r4294538e93ac"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: preference — предпочтение; advice — совет; consequence — последствие; urgent — срочный."},{"id":"168b3a88-86c5-5d91-bc63-dc395b9d2219","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что следует из предупреждения менеджера?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"Two colleagues were choosing how to reach a training centre after heavy rain. One said she would rather take the train than drive. The other preferred driving because of the equipment they needed to carry. Before deciding, their manager warned that the main road might be flooded and said they had better check the travel updates. The advice did not remove their choice of transport, but it made checking the conditions important before acting on either preference.","options":[{"id":"vf5acd48e0522","label":"They should check conditions before choosing how to travel."},{"id":"v513550bffb04","label":"Driving has been conclusively prohibited everywhere."},{"id":"v624e53ad578a","label":"The train is guaranteed to have room for all equipment."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf5acd48e0522"},"reference_answer":"vf5acd48e0522","incorrect_answer":"v513550bffb04","explanation":"Совет не устанавливает всеобщий запрет или гарантию другого варианта."},{"id":"700d158b-9b89-5dc7-9472-1677bced4bbd","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Вырази предпочтение дождаться отчёта.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Would you like to decide now?"}],"options":[{"id":"v505139707dd5","label":"I had rather waiting the report."},{"id":"v8ec9d945a070","label":"I would rather wait for the inspection report."},{"id":"v6a7309161802","label":"I would rather to wait for the inspection report."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8ec9d945a070"},"reference_answer":"v8ec9d945a070","incorrect_answer":"v6a7309161802","explanation":"Would rather wait — стандартная конструкция предпочтения."},{"id":"7b34a765-dad8-5fff-a059-5f3c35d1f56b","lesson_id":"53927c28-9fea-5aa3-96ec-7fa75692fe16","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A matter requiring prompt attention is ___.","options":[{"id":"v0f0a5f602f71","label":"urgent"},{"id":"v2d4da1121e64","label":"optional in every circumstance"},{"id":"v954cc2260b87","label":"retrospective"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0f0a5f602f71"},"reference_answer":"v0f0a5f602f71","in